.TH FHICL-GETPAR 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2ebintools v1_01_21" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
fhicl-getpar \- print one parameter of a FHiCL configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fhicl-getpar
.RB { \-\-string | \-\-int | \-\-strlist | \-\-keys }
.I name
.I file.fcl
.br
.B fhicl-getpar
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fhicl-getpar
parses
.I file.fcl
with fhiclcpp, builds the complete
.B fhicl::ParameterSet
(includes resolved, prolog dropped, references substituted) and prints the
value of the fully qualified, dot-separated parameter
.IR name ,
for example
.B physics.producers
or
.BR services.TFileService.fileName .
It is intended for shell scripts that need one value from an art job
configuration without running art.
.PP
The arguments are strictly positional: exactly three, in the order option,
name, file.
The type option decides how the value is decoded and printed:
.TP
.B \-\-string
Decode as
.B std::string
and print it on one line.
.TP
.B \-\-int
Decode as a C++
.B int
and print it on one line.
A value that is not an integer, or does not fit in an
.BR int ,
is an error.
.TP
.B \-\-strlist
Decode a sequence as a list of strings and print one element per line.
.TP
.B \-\-keys
Decode a table and print the names of its immediate members, one per
line, in the order returned by
.BR fhicl::ParameterSet::get_names() .
.PP
There is no option for floating-point or boolean values; for those use
.B \-\-string
or
.BR fhicl-dump (1).
.PP
.I file.fcl
itself is opened as given, relative to the current directory or as an
absolute path.
Files it
.BR #include s
are looked up along
.B FHICL_FILE_PATH
(the
.B cet::filepath_lookup_after1
policy).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-string ", " \-\-int ", " \-\-strlist ", " \-\-keys
Value type, as above.
Must be the first argument.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage line to standard output and exit 0.
Recognised only as the first argument.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I file.fcl
The top-level configuration to parse.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FHICL_FILE_PATH
Colon-separated list of directories searched for files named in
.B #include
directives.
What happens when it is unset is determined by
.B cet::search_path
in the cetlib version the program is linked against; set it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The value was printed, or
.B \-h
was given.
.TP
.B 1
Any error, with a message on standard error: wrong number of arguments
or unknown option (the usage line is appended), the file cannot be found
or parsed, the parameter is absent, or its value cannot be decoded as the
requested type.
.PP
An absent parameter and an unreadable file both exit 1, so the status
alone does not tell a script which happened.
.SH EXAMPLES
Print the process name and the producer labels of a job:
.PP
.RS
.EX
export FHICL_FILE_PATH=.:/path/to/fcl/tree
fhicl-getpar \-\-string process_name job.fcl
fhicl-getpar \-\-keys physics.producers job.fcl
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use a value in a script, falling back to a default when it cannot be read:
.PP
.RS
.EX
out=$(fhicl-getpar \-\-string services.TFileService.fileName job.fcl \e
      2>/dev/null) || out=hist.root
.EE
.RE
.PP
List the trigger paths:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fhicl-getpar \-\-strlist physics.trigger_paths job.fcl
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fhicl-summary (1),
.BR fhicl-dump (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrei Gaponenko (2015), based on
.B parsefhicl.cc
by Rob Kutschke.
